<title>UK: Ex-dividends take 1.109 points off UK's FTSE index.</title>
<headline>Ex-dividends take 1.109 points off UK's FTSE index.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>FTSE International said the following FTSE 100 stocks went ex-dividend on Monday and the effect was to take 1.109 points off the index in early trading.</p>
<p>				     DIVIDEND   INDEX</p>
<p>				     (PENCE)    EFFECT</p>
<p>COMPANY				Net	 Net</p>
<p> * British Land		    6.08     0.164</p>
<p> * Dixons Group		    8.10     0.195</p>
<p> * Grand Metropolitan	    6.25     0.750</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
